   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to making care and\nservices provided by licensed clinical social workers eligible for coverage\nunder the Medicaid program",
    "basePrintNo": "S5960",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5960-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 42,
       "fullName": "Jen Metzger",
       "imgName": "1054_Jen_Metzger.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1234,
       "sessionMemberId": 1232,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "METZGER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §365-a, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5960\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the social services law, in relation\nto making care and services provided by licensed clinical social workers\neligible for coverage under the Medicaid program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nMakes care and services provided by licensed clinical social workers\neligible for coverage under Medicaid.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends Subdivision 2 of section 365-a of the social services law to\nclinical social workers licensed pursuant to Article 154 of the Educa-\ntion law to bill Medicaid directly for their services within their scope\nof practice.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would allow Licensed Clinical Social Workers to directly bill\nMedicaid for their services. Licensed Clinical Social Workers represent\nthe largest group of mental health practitioners in the nation. They are\noften the first to diagnose and treat people with mental disorders and\nvarious emotional and behavioral disturbances.  Clinical Social Workers\nare essential to a variety of client-centered settings, including commu-\nnity mental health centers, hospitals, substance use treatment and\nrecovery programs, schools, primary health care centers, child welfare\nagencies, aging services, employee assistance programs, and private\npractice settings.\n\nLicensed Clinical Social Work has a primary focus on the emotional, and\nmental health of individuals, couples, families, and groups and by defi-\nnition, includes the scope of practice of the LMSW, diagnosis of mental,\nemotional, behavioral, addictive and developmental disorders and disa-\nbilities, the development and implementation of appropriate assessment-\nbased treatment plans; and the provision of crisis oriented psychothera-\npy, including brief, short-term and long-term psychotherapy and\npsychotherapeutic treatment. in addition, given their unique training,\nLCSW's are the only licensed mental health professionals that assess the\nperson-in-environment, a practice-guiding principle that highlights the\nimportance of understanding an individual and individual behavior in\nlight of the environmental contexts in which that person lives and acts\n(family finances, connections, living situation, religion, employment,\netc.,) Further, Article 163 of the Education Law authorizes a qualified\nLCSW to practice mental health counseling, marriage and family therapy,\ncreative arts therapy or psychoanalysis. Given the breadth of the above,\nclearly, LCSW's are a vital component of the community mental health\nsystem and as such, should have authorization to directly bill Medicaid\nfor their services, thus broadening access to crucial mental health\nservices.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019 Session - new bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n90th day after becoming law\n",
